# .dockerignore — the build context sent to the daemon.
#
# This file did not exist before 2026-09, which cost three things:
#
#   1. CORRECTNESS. The Dockerfile runs `yarn install` and then
#      `COPY frontend/ ./`. With no ignore file that COPY dropped the
#      HOST's 1.3 GB node_modules on top of the freshly installed Linux
#      one — macOS-built binaries over a linux/amd64 image.
#   2. SECRETS. `COPY backend/ /app/backend/` carried backend/.env (real
#      OPENROUTER / AZURE / GEMINI keys) into a layer. The later
#      `RUN rm -f /app/backend/.env` deletes it from the final filesystem
#      but NOT from image history — `docker save` still yields the keys.
#      Excluding it here is what actually keeps it out.
#   3. SIZE. The context was 1.6 GB, so every build re-uploaded .venv,
#      .git and the whole node_modules tree before Docker did any work.
#
# Keep the exclusions below in sync with what the Dockerfile actually
# COPYs: frontend/{package.json,yarn.lock,src,public,*.config.js,tsconfig.json},
# backend/**.py + requirements.txt, and docker/.

# ── Secrets — never in a layer ────────────────────────────────────────
# The runtime .env is written by docker/entrypoint.sh from the compose
# `environment:` block. Nothing here is needed at build time.
# Every .env at any depth, including the root one — it is read by
# `docker compose` off the host filesystem, never from the build context,
# so excluding it here changes nothing about compose.
**/.env
**/.env.*
certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# ── Dependency trees — installed inside the image, never copied ───────
# node_modules in particular MUST be excluded: it is copied after
# `yarn install` and would clobber the correct linux/amd64 install.
**/node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
backend/venv/
wheels/

# ── Build output — stage 1 produces its own ───────────────────────────
frontend/build/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ── Python bytecode and tool caches ───────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md: local .pyc are built by the 3.14 dev venv and will not match
# the image's 3.11. Harmless (Python skips mismatched magic numbers) but
# pure waste and confusing when debugging inside the container.
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/coverage/

# ── VCS and editor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# ── Agent / tooling state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
memory/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
HUMAN_INTERVENTION.md
LEDGER.md

# ── Docs, reports and design assets — not runtime inputs ──────────────
docs/
architecture/
test_reports/
*.md
!README.md
*.pptx
*.pdf

# ── Docker's own files (the Dockerfile COPYs docker/ explicitly) ──────
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# ── Local runtime state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The embedded Qdrant store (QDRANT_PATH). Host data, never an image input.
.qdrant_local/

# ── Local scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.bak
*.bak2
*.save
*_old
*_backup
tmp/
.tmp/
